{"title":"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #6</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #8</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Tuesday’s high temperature was 4 C warmer than that of Monday’s. Wednesday’s high temperature\nwas 6 C cooler than that of Monday’s. If Tuesday’s high temperature was 22 C, what was\nWednesday’s high temperature?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d135616355bb771dce1b4fc690526c8b0c4edee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)} 20 \\quad\\text{(B)} 24\\quad \\text{(C)} 12\\quad \\text{(D)} 32 \\quad \\text{(E)} 16 \\quad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"281\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>(all in Celsius)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Tuesday's high temperature was 22 C, so Monday's high temperature was 18 C and Wednesday's temperature was 12 C.\n</p><p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/c/71c2a4722ee063b7a4982ff5eaf9b97de930c4b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(C)} \\quad 12}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"74\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>-edited by coolmath34\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.p